<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    HOME-SCREEN-WIDGET FEATURE (Part 1/2).

    minWidth/minHeight ("2x1" cells at the common 74dp/cell approximation) is
    the *small* quick-connect-button size; minResizeWidth/minResizeHeight let
    the user shrink it no further than that single-row card, while
    targetCellWidth/targetCellHeight (API 31+, ignored pre-31 same as
    previewLayout below) describe the larger *default* placement — a 3x3
    list — that most launchers actually drop on the home screen when the
    widget is first added. resizeMode="horizontal|vertical" is what makes
    the widget resizable in both directions in the first place: dragging it
    anywhere between minWidth/minHeight and the full list size is what
    HexRdpAppWidgetProvider.onAppWidgetOptionsChanged() reacts to by
    swapping between widget_quick_connect_small.xml and
    widget_connections_list.xml — see that method's chooseLayout() doc
    comment for the exact size thresholds.

    updatePeriodMillis="0": this widget is never redrawn on a dumb timer —
    every redraw is pushed explicitly by WidgetUpdater.requestUpdate*() right
    when something it displays actually changed (profile added/edited/
    deleted, isConnected flipped, isFavorite toggled), the same reasoning
    QuickConnectTileService's ACTIVE_TILE-less design already documents for
    the Quick Settings tile.

    android:configure requires WidgetConfigureActivity to be BOTH declared
    in AndroidManifest.xml with the ACTION_APPWIDGET_CONFIGURE intent-filter
    AND exported — this xml resource alone does not make the widget
    configurable; see the manifest comment for that activity.

    HOME-SCREEN-WIDGET FEATURE (Part 2/2): previewLayout points at
    widget_preview.xml, not the real widget_connections_list.xml used by
    initialLayout above — the real layout's ListView has no adapter bound
    when the system's "Add widget" picker inflates it (nothing in this app
    is running at that point to call setRemoteAdapter()), so it would always
    render as the empty state. widget_preview.xml is a static mock with
    hardcoded example rows instead, purely for a representative picker
    preview — see its own doc comment.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="110dp"
    android:minHeight="40dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="110dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="40dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:targetCellHeight="3"
    android:maxResizeWidth="300dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="300dp"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_connections_list"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_preview"
    android:previewImage="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
    android:configure="com.systemsgo.hex.widget.WidgetConfigureActivity"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:description="@string/widget_description" />
